First Author: Peyster
Title: An automated computational image analysis pipeline for histological grading of cardiac allograft rejection
Source number: 69

Very short summary: This retrospective multicenter diagnostic study included 2,472 endomyocardial-biopsy slides from 546 heart transplant recipients at three US centers. The interpretable CACHE-Grader used hand-crafted quantitative histologic features and support vector machines to classify cellular rejection; on 1,447 independent validation slides, the binary model achieved an AUC of 0.92, 84.5% agreement, 85% sensitivity, and 84% specificity, while the four-grade model achieved 65.9% agreement.

