	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: The pipeline extracted 154 biologically inspired, hand-crafted histologic features describing lymphocyte foci, tissue compartments, densities, and spatial interactions. Support vector machine classifiers were selected for binary low- versus high-grade rejection (M1) and four-grade rejection classification (M2). Features were ranked using a Wilcoxon rank-sum test for M1 and a t-test for M2, resulting in models with 2 and 15 features, respectively. Validation included 395 held-out slides from the development center and 1,052 geographically external slides from two other centers; no explicit SVM hyperparameter-search procedure was reported.

