	•	Training Size (N): 911
	•	Test Size (N): 1447
	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Slides underwent automated HistoQC assessment, stain deconvolution, tiling, K-means tissue segmentation, lymphocyte-cluster detection, and feature normalization relative to tissue-compartment size. The authors deliberately enriched the cohort for grades 2R/3R to approximately 20%, compared with approximately 8% in routine practice, to ensure sufficient high-grade cases; this addressed imbalance through cohort construction rather than algorithmic weighting or resampling. The training set contained 911 slides, and the composite validation set contained 1,447 slides: 395 internal and 1,052 external. Missing-feature imputation was not described. Source code was publicly available through the CACHE-Grader repository.

