	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: Values refer to the binary M1 classifier for low-grade 0R/1R versus high-grade 2R/3R rejection in the composite independent validation set. It achieved 84.5% agreement with the grade of record, AUC 0.92, sensitivity 0.85, and specificity 0.84; no AUC confidence interval was reported. The four-grade M2 classifier achieved 65.9% agreement (95% CI 63.4–68.3%), with similar internal and external agreement of 66.1% and 65.8%. Numeric PPV, NPV, F1-score, formal probabilistic calibration metrics, and DCA were not reported.

